Source mechanism on pinnedf64
bbt-supervisor/src/supervisor.rs:314–329 — ordinary Recorder.update uses try_lock; collisions increment missed and skip the update.
bbt-supervisor/src/supervisor.rs:356–405 — snapshot holds that buffer mutex while copying totals, seats and8192 retained spans.
bbt-mux/tests/checkpoint_scheduling.rs:209–215/:240–269 — row() reads only recorder seats; catch_up uses parsed_byte_end as its sole liveness clock and completion conjunction. It never asks authoritative worker state on timeout.
bbt-mux/src/logic.rs:3715–3735 — live Event applies to Playback first, then publishes sequence/cumulative parse stats; parsed_byte_end/checkpoint fields are separately copied at record_checkpoint_state:3613–3626. Partial field observations and dropped last updates are not a liveness oracle.
bbt-supervisor/src/ring.rs:300–335 — Playback requires contiguous event sequence and increments byte_end by actual Output bytes; event coalescer preserves the newest Event payload and supervisor flush_output retains it. No empty-payload notification substitution was found.

